From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:59:51 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 186/207] runner: opt-in abstain records (PREFIX_ABSTAINS) name
 every abstained cell, its source, reason and decision point

T1's census could not attribute 40 of 276 abstains: runner.cells records only owned writes. With PREFIX_ABSTAINS=1
(default 0, effective with CELLS) the final receipt adds abstain_schema 1 and one record per abstain (T1's
ABSTAIN-RECORDS-T1-SPEC field names): cell, form, lang, code, span_sha256/span_len, prior notebook cells, display,
source_field/at/end (the code's last exact copy before its close; null when normalized, e.g. REPL prompts) and
source_close_at, program_kind, backend_route, stage, reason, error_name, resume_field/at/token, round,
next_decision_token, reply_tokens, owned_tokens 0, steps, held_ms; then abstains_complete, abstains_dropped,
abstain_frontend_detail false and runner_config. Reasons: context; the frontend's tags; out_of_memory; backend_abstain,
budget, fault; empty_output, multiline_output, mark_value_shape, token_cap, trace_shape. Records go only into the
final receipt, never the live notes, so stream deltas are unchanged; off, the receipt is byte-identical.

Not exported (the frontend gives the runner only its abstain tag): op, op_families, plan width, width state, route
attempts. No artifact hashes.

test-runner-abstain-host: each reason forced on the lane host (source bytes, resume anchors, conservation, on/off
identity), every frontend tag, a mixed session (last copy, normalized source, next decision, dropped means
incomplete), and the knob (default off, 2 refused, cells off means none).

(cherry picked from commit 571f1832627773e3f3ab326ba8af1a4582720e0d)
